WEBVTT

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:21.390
This can't be happening; I clasp my head in my hands

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:27.980
As I struggle with my desire to escape from this saturated world.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:33.400
Time goes flowing past with the rustling roar of sand.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.820
Things never get any better.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.740
I'm gazing on toward a dreamless tomorrow.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:47.040
I want to bid farewell to my days of constantly feeling lost.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.510
I try stretching out my hand in resistance.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:58.260
We'll cry millions upon millions of tears, then be reborn.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:04.390
Let's keep going, with red in our eyes, toward the future we drew for ourselves.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:10.150
Come over to me; I'm clapping my hands.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.110
Who are you? Where are you coming from?

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:16.450
I strain my eyes in the darkness.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:22.030
I can't see a thing, and nothing makes sense, but I'll go anyway.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:28.540
To the place where you're waiting, lit by a beacon of light.

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.760
As to be expected from the "Defeated Detective".

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:40.460
Or maybe I should be calling you the "Great Detective".

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.720
Why do something like this?

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.270
I'm a novelist.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.540
A novelist?

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:48.690
I write novels.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:52.120
Not with a pen... but with reality.

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.130
Following the deductions of the "Great Detective",

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.120
all mysteries are brought to light!

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:59.230
I expected that Yajima would kill his own wife.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.780
Why would you try to make that happen?

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:06.540
Because that's the role of the "Great Detective".

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.590
No matter how cruel the outcome,

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:13.020
to wait until all of the victims have met their deaths, then bring forth his deductions:

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.300
that is the "Great Detective".

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.040
No matter how tragic his reasons,

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.340
to expose everything in the light of day:

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:21.110
that is the "Great Detective".

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:23.780
I have chosen you...

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:26.810
...as this world's final "Great Detective".

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:28.810
You... chose me?

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:33.680
Yes! You are my very own "Great Detective"!

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:35.350
What is it you want?

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:39.170
There's no need for worry, I'm a novelist;

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:41.320
I don't care for anything other than writing stories.

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:48.200
However, I don't write upon paper; I write upon reality.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:52.580
If you turn reality into a story...

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:04.370
Come alive, "Great Detective"!

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:05.850
Solve the mystery!

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:18.230
Somebody...!

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:40.170
War...

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:42.170
That's good!

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:54.060
Yuuki-chan, what are you doing?

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:55.640
Look, over there!

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:56.560
Over there?

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:00.740
Yuuki-san, the director asked me to get you for him!

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:03.490
What the heck, have you been slacking off again?

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:06.840
You're quite the celebrity to have an actress coming to fetch you!

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.740
Ah, sorry! I'll go right away.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:17.460
Shinjuurou-kun, you're late!

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:20.210
This guy was over by the planes.

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.430
I knew it...

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:23.870
What do you mean, "You knew", Motoko-chan?

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:26.720
Men always love special effects.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:29.090
Even my dad...

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:31.250
My dad?

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.380
What is it, Motoko-chan?

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:35.940
It's nothing.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:38.110
And neither of you are allowed to add "chan" to my name.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:41.230
What are you all doing over there?!

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:44.810
He looks mad. Shall we get started?

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:46.080
Is your make-up ready?

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:47.700
I can go without it.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:51.200
If I end up looking bad, it's because you suck at your job!

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:53.830
Let's do our best.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:56.580
Please make me look beautiful.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.220
Director, are we ready?

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:11.010
No enthusiasm, as usual...

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.640
I'll just go when I'm ready, then.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.390
Sayo-san, I'm sure you have a boyfriend!

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:20.090
But Sumie-san looks like a princess-type,

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.740
you don't seem like you've ever been with a man.

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:24.530
What are you saying all of a sudden, Motoko-chan?!

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.290
I told you not to add the "chan"!

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:29.880
After all, I want to get to know the two of you better!

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:37.090
The three of us all escaped to here, fleeing from different places.

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:40.240
We were all taken in by the man who
owns this room, and decided to live here.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:43.960
The man equally lo...

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:45.400
Loved us?

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:46.840
That!

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:50.910
But on a certain day, he disappeared...

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.680
...and the three of us are wandering through the burning city.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:59.230
But I heard that the director hasn't decided on the last scene.

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:02.780
We don't even know if we'll be able to reunite with the man.

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:05.460
I wonder if all four of us will be able to live happily together again.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.300
I don't want that at all!

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.210
I want him to properly choose one amongst the three of us!

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:11.270
Oh my...

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:13.830
W-Why are you laughing?

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.660
Hey... C'mon!

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:20.070
They sure seem happy.

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:21.960
Don't you think so, Director?

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:04.450
Solve the mystery.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:06.340
Mystery?

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:09.590
It hurts... It really hurts!

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:13.580
It's hot... Red...

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:16.680
I'm... So hot!

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:23.560
We're gonna die... We're all gonna die!

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:36.330
That's good!

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:47.010
I wonder why...

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:49.270
Why do I have to solve the mystery?

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:52.490
Nothing has even occurred...

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:56.590
If a war were to really break out, I don't think I'd make it out alive...

00:07:56.590 --> 00:07:58.020
You're probably right...

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:58.820
Why?

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:01.530
'Cause I've never even imagined it...

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:04.010
If bombs really came falling from the sky,

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:05.100
I'd have no idea what to do.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.830
That's true...

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:10.610
We haven't seen a war since before my grandfather's time.

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.480
There hasn't ever been a war.

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:18.210
No one loses the ones they love, or has their homes burned down.

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:19.990
There's no one thinking sorrowful thoughts.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.400
That's why we're able to do things like make movies, right?

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:34.880
I'd really like to do that scene over after all.

00:08:35.350 --> 00:08:36.290
Why?

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:39.270
I felt like I was losing to Sayo!

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:40.880
I can do better!

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:42.720
Ah, Director! I wanted to ask-

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:46.150
Yuuki Shinjuurou! What are you slacking off for?

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:49.370
Directer, would we be able to do another take?

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:52.650
Do you even get it? I'm the director!

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:54.950
Don't go causing me trouble!

00:08:57.380 --> 00:09:01.080
Director, I want to do all I can for them...

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:03.200
Don't talk to them.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:03.910
Get it?

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:05.660
I'll kill you.

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:14.260
Good work today!

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:35.320
Where... am I?

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:40.320
That's right, I had something to ask the director.

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:43.580
There's some mystery within this movie...

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:45.380
Something is strange about it...

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:54.870
You get it, don't you?! You're a beautiful butterfly!

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:56.000
I don't know...

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:57.130
Wait!

00:09:57.690 --> 00:09:59.220
You can't!

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:01.570
Don't tell anyone! Please, don't!

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:03.130
Let go of me!

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:04.970
Please, just listen to me!

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:09.580
Tomorrow, right here. You must come.

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:23.880
What are you doing, Yuuki?

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:24.790
Get back to your room.

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:28.730
What were you doing, Director?

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:30.540
None of your business!

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:40.710
The camera work in this movie has been entrusted to me.

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:44.940
For many days now, I've been recording a film that targets high-brow audiences,

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:48.640
where modern Japan is pulled into war.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:54.900
Which of the actresses was there with the director?

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:02.610
There's a mystery within this scene.

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:04.940
The mystery will be solved.

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:08.270
The truth must be exposed.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:16.450
There wasn't a war.

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:41.400
JJ... Systems...

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:53.290
Mamori... Kaze?

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:55.730
Shinjuurou-sama!

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:16.490
Director!

00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:17.060
What?

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.420
About last night...

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:24.520
Mitaka-san? Rosenberg and Schaffner are this way.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:33.460
Is this a mystery as well?

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:43.880
They're kinda out of sync...

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.890
Is the director okay with this?

00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:56.590
It's so hot!

00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:58.270
Ah! I found some shade!

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:03.000
Yuuki Shinjuurou... are you looking at women again?

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:05.820
Yeah... you're referring to the actresses?

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:08.410
Tanimura and Yada are over there, right?

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:10.280
Izawa, too?

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:11.550
Yes.

00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:28.480
What's wrong?

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:29.880
Yuuki-san!

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:34.370
I had something I wanted to ask the director about the script, but...

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:37.090
The last part of the script isn't written, so we asked him,

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:40.520
"Will we all go somewhere?"

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:45.070
And he responded, saying, "You won't be going anywhere; you're all sinners!"

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:47.570
Do you think so too, Shinjuurou-kun?

00:13:48.020 --> 00:13:51.660
We have no idea who we are or where we're from...

00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:54.140
...to end without any place to go is just too...

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.340
There was this line...

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:58.080
Is not war but a toy?

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:00.240
I'm not the only one who thinks this;

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:03.960
You... You too, have been treating war as a toy.

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:08.390
We should have tried to get more out of the war.

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:12.890
We should have clung to the war
until we were battered and bruised...

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:15.900
...sucked it dry... entwined ourselves with it...

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:20.230
Those are the lines we say when we hear that the war has ended.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:22.230
So, what about them?

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:26.320
All three of us have a different interpretation of their meaning.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:30.210
Um, I think that if the war were over,

00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:34.740
we should be happy that our lives will be returning to normal.

00:14:35.320 --> 00:14:39.000
That's why it bothered me and I wanted to ask the director the meaning of it.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:39.750
But that's not it!

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:42.640
There's no meaning in living a normal life.

00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:45.800
With the war, and us running around like crazy,

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:50.370
aren't we supposed to have finally learned what it means to be alive?

00:14:51.230 --> 00:14:54.380
Our existence becomes close to that of a beasts,

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:56.380
knowing only life and survival...

00:14:56.380 --> 00:15:00.130
...but meeting that special person and being able to...

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:00.980
Love one another.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:01.650
That!

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:05.540
I feel like I understand, or... What should I say...

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:09.080
I guess I'd like to try living at that fine line,

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:11.910
and I feel like constantly living an ordinary life is something terrible...

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:15.480
I suppose I'm a bit different.

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:19.910
I feel as if we're all being judged by the war.

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:21.590
Being judged?

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:25.610
Good people and bad people all die the same way, don't they?

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:29.550
For us to be sinners... I wonder if that's the meaning?

00:15:29.550 --> 00:15:31.600
You're all overthinking it!

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:32.800
This is a movie!

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:35.720
What are you saying, Shinjuurou-kun?!

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:38.180
If that's the case, why make a movie like this?

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:42.120
For what purpose are we all fleeing amidst some imaginary war?!

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:46.830
So that we can learn just how precious our uninspirational,

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:49.300
boring, ordinary lives truly are.

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:50.240
That's not it!

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:52.710
Everyone's actually hoping...

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:57.630
...that, even if it's not a war, something
grand will happen and help change them...

00:15:57.630 --> 00:16:00.250
...that they'll be able to find something precious!

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:06.340
But, if someone loses their home or
family to a volcanic eruption, or fire,

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:08.750
don't they naturally wish to have their ordinary lives back?

00:16:10.510 --> 00:16:14.270
But there are also people who simply enjoy observing eruptions and fires.

00:16:14.270 --> 00:16:17.050
Even knowing that it brings sorrow,

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:22.620
we wish for things that destroy our world, ourselves...

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:26.520
I'm wondering if that's why we must be judged for it...

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:31.050
I see.

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:33.280
The mystery that is a movie.

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:34.930
Shinjuurou-san?

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:35.930
Are you listening?

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:39.280
Hey, which of us do you think is right?

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:45.410
If you'd like, I can ask the director about the last part, then try writing it out.

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:48.670
We may find an answer that way.

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:49.900
Really?!

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:50.840
Yeah.

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:56.250
C'mon, lunch break is almost over!

00:16:56.250 --> 00:16:57.680
Okay!

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:05.140
But this line used to be...

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:09.360
Thank you!

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:11.560
That's what I told you!

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:32.340
Even if that girl was one of the three of them,

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:35.510
they're all living earnestly.

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:37.780
They're betting everything on this movie.

00:17:58.510 --> 00:18:01.030
Director! What is the meaning of this?!

00:18:01.030 --> 00:18:02.530
Are you trying to ruin everything?!

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:04.280
Huh?

00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:06.660
What the hell is in your hand?

00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:37.280
What... is this?

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:46.250
Hey! What happened?

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:48.630
The director is...

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:56.570
It's as if he was hit by a train...

00:18:56.570 --> 00:19:00.150
But that train is just part of the set. It's made of papier-mâché.

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:01.390
It can't even move.

00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:05.620
Apparently, no one saw Mitaka-san after mealtime.

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:09.920
So... The last person to have met with him was... me?

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:13.150
But why did they have to kill him?

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:15.440
There's only one person with a motive.

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:18.320
Someone angry at Director Mitaka...

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:20.930
Someone who thought he was going to ruin the movie,

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:24.850
along with the efforts of these girls... Me.

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:29.290
Yuuki-san?

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:31.330
It's possible that I...

00:19:35.490 --> 00:19:36.960
What kinds of things have you been dreaming up?

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:39.500
The story's all make-believe anyway!

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:40.470
It's a lie!

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:41.760
That's not true!

00:20:07.670 --> 00:20:10.770
Yuuki-san, that's enough already! C'mon!

00:20:12.530 --> 00:20:13.750
It won't stop!

00:20:14.240 --> 00:20:16.170
Someone's telling me to solve the mystery!

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:19.880
If I assemble all the clues and make a deduction,

00:20:20.310 --> 00:20:21.860
the criminal is...

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:22.930
...there's no one but me.

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:25.230
That's what we call a confession, isn't it?

00:20:33.970 --> 00:20:35.900
Have I met you somewhere?

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:39.310
I'm Kaishou, of the Metropolitan Police Dept.

00:20:39.310 --> 00:20:44.360
I'm arresting you on suspicion of
murdering Director Mitaka Kichitarou!

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:08.390
Wandering hazily on a pale morning, hearing a whispered prayer,

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:16.350
You and I trace a twisted scenery.

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:24.030
We're seeking the (truth). "We don't even care if it's a lie."

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:28.410
As if we can see right through it,

00:21:30.490 --> 00:21:32.370
We follow it along.

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:36.330
Looking for, going beyond words,

00:21:36.410 --> 00:21:40.340
Like a falling feather.

00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:43.460
Looking for, find it,

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:49.800
So we can come closer together.

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:08.320
Looking for, unravel it,

00:22:08.320 --> 00:22:12.330
Tear it apart, like a cloud.

00:22:12.330 --> 00:22:15.410
Looking for, find it,

00:22:16.370 --> 00:22:20.250
So we can come closer together.

00:22:23.180 --> 00:22:27.480
C'mon already! Let me see Shinjuurou!

00:22:27.480 --> 00:22:28.170
Hey!

00:22:32.860 --> 00:22:34.470
What should we do, Kazamori?

00:22:41.620 --> 00:22:44.110
I can smell her scent close-by...

00:22:51.950 --> 00:22:54.990
Hey, that's all the screen time I get?!

00:22:54.990 --> 00:22:56.380
What's the idea?!

00:22:56.380 --> 00:22:59.610
Do you know what'll happen if you make me angry?!

00:22:59.610 --> 00:23:03.620
Look, part of the next episode was inspired by "The Election Murder",

00:23:03.620 --> 00:23:07.400
and if you read the story first, it gives you all kinds of spoilers!

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:09.050
Should I spill? Should I talk? Should I give the game away here?!

00:23:09.050 --> 00:23:09.740
Okay, actually...

00:23:09.740 --> 00:23:11.430
Ah, K-Kazamori!

00:23:11.430 --> 00:23:13.800
Stop! O-Okay! I won't do it!

00:23:13.800 --> 00:23:15.810
Next time on UN-GO: "The King of Paradise".

00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:18.030
S-Stop it, Kazamori!!
